r.com)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Introduction\nWelcome to WeTransfer. We respect your privacy and are committed to protecting your personal data. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you visit our website ([https://wetransfer.com/](https://wetransfer.com/)) or use our file-sharing and transfer services. \n\nPlease read this Privacy Policy carefully. If you do not agree with the terms of this Privacy Policy, please do not access or use our services.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Information We Collect\nWe collect information that identifies, relates to, describes, references, or can be linked, directly or indirectly, with a particular consumer or device (\"Personal Data\"). Depending on how you interact with WeTransfer, we may collect the following categories of information:\n\n*   **Information You Provide Voluntarily:** Email addresses (of senders and recipients), messages included with transfers, account registration details (if applicable), and support inquiries submitted through our help center.\n*   **Automatically Collected Technical Data:** When you access our website, our servers and content delivery networks (including our Next.js-based infrastructure via `cdn.wetransfer.com`) automatically record information. This may include your IP address, browser type, operating system, referring URLs, access times, and pages viewed.\n*   **File Metadata:** Information related to the files you upload for transfer, such as file size, names, and transfer timestamps.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Cookies and Tracking Technologies\nWe use cookies, web beacons, pixels, and similar tracking technologies to collect and track information regarding your activity on our website to enhance your user experience, analyze traffic patterns, and deliver optimized content.\n\n*   **Essential Cookies:** Required for the operation of our website and core file-transfer services.\n*   **Analytics and Performance Cookies:** Help us understand how visitors interact with our website by collecting and reporting information anonymously (utilized via our application scripts hosted on our CDN).\n\nYou can instruct your browser to refuse all cookies or to indicate when a cookie is being sent. However, if you do not accept cookies, some parts of our service (such as core file-upload mechanisms or security scripts) may not function properly.\n\n---\n\n## 4. How We Use Your Information\nWe use the information we collect for various business purposes, including:\n*   Providing, maintaining, and improving our file-sharing and transfer services.\n*   Processing and delivering file transfers between senders and recipients.\n*   Monitoring technical functionality, protecting against security risks, and debugging system errors (such as firewall or browser-blocking issues).\n*   Responding to customer service inquiries and providing support via our help center.\n*   Complying with legal obligations and enforcing our terms of service.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Third-Party Services and Content\nOur website utilizes scripts, content delivery networks (CDNs), and technological infrastructure (e.g., hosted assets via `cdn.wetransfer.com`) to deliver content efficiently. While we strive to protect your data, interactions with third-party links, plug-ins, or embedded content are governed by the privacy policies of those third parties, not this Privacy Policy.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Data Security\nWe implement appropriate technical and organizational security measures designed to protect the security of any personal information we process. However, please note that no electronic transmission over the Internet or information storage technology can be guaranteed to be 100% secure. Always ensure you are using secure networks and up-to-date browsers when transferring files.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Your Data Protection Rights (GDPR, CCPA, and DPDP)\nDepending on your geographic location (such as the European Economic Area under the GDPR, California under the CCPA, or India under the DPDP), you may have certain statutory rights regarding your personal data:\n\n*   **Right to Access:** You have the right to request copies of your personal data.\n*   **Right to Rectification:** You have the right to request that we correct any information you believe is inaccurate or complete information you believe is incomplete.\n*   **Right to Erasure:** You have the right to request that we erase your personal data, under certain conditions.\n*   **Right to Restrict / Object to Processing:** You have the right to object to or restrict our processing of your personal data.\n*   **Right to Data Portability:** You have the right to request that we transfer the data that we have collected to another organization, or directly to you, under certain conditions.\n\nTo exercise any of these rights, please submit a request to our privacy team at [privacy@wetransfer.com](mailto:privacy@wetransfer.com).\n\n---\n\n## 8. Children\'s Privacy\nOur services are not directed to individuals under the age of 16. We do not knowingly collect personal identifiable information from children under 16. If you become aware that a child has provided us with personal data, please contact us immediately at [privacy@wetransfer.com](mailto:privacy@wetransfer.com), and we will take steps to remove such information.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Changes to This Privacy Policy\nWe may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page and updating the \"Effective Date\" at the top. You are advised to review this Privacy Policy periodically for any changes.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Contact Us\nIf you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please contact us at:\n\n*   **Company:** WeTransfer\n*   **Email:** [privacy@wetransfer.com](mailto:privacy@wetransfer.com)\n*   **Help Center / Support:** Accessible via [/help-center](https://wetransfer.com/help-center)', '2026-11-23 02:41:20');
